        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Odysseas Elytis, Cornel West, David Connolly, Nikiforos Vrettakos, Kiki Dimoula, Nikos Engonopoulos\n- Works: Race Matters\n- Concepts: romantic modernism\n- Organizations: Democratic Socialists of America\n\nFacts:\n- Odysseas Elytis, the pen name of Odysseas Alepoudellis, was born on 2 November 1911 and died on 18 March 1996.\n- Odysseas Elytis was regarded as a major exponent of romantic modernism in Greece and internationally.\n- Cornel West was born on June 2, 1953.\n- Cornel West is an American philosopher, political activist, social critic, author, and public intellectual.\n- Cornel West is a prominent member of the Democratic Socialists of America.\n- David Connolly has translated poetry and novels from Greek to English.\n- David Connolly has translated writing by Nikiforos Vrettakos, Odysseas Elytis, Kiki Dimoula, and Nikos Engonopoulos.\n- Race Matters is a social sciences book by Cornel West.",
